Q: R Shiny: how to eagerly update output from within an iteration A: <p><em>using the <code>shinyjs</code> package and shinjs::html(), the effect on the textOutput is immediate even from inside the loop</em> as per <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/69917804/28479453">this answer</a></p>
<pre><code>library(shiny)
library(shinyjs)

shinyApp(
  ui = shinyUI(fluidPage(useShinyjs(), textOutput(&quot;log&quot;))), 
  server = \(input, output) {
    Map(f = \(x) {
      Sys.sleep(.1)
      shinyjs::html(id = 'log', paste0(&quot;iteration: &quot;, x))
    }, 1:5)
})
</code></pre>
